- Produce a structured 8-step analyst output (DELTA, PRIORITIZE, HYPOTHESES, SELF-CRITIQUE, NEXT ACTION, LEARNING, RISK SCORE) for ongoing automated bug bounty hunting across Google VRP and MSRC programs, using a massive accumulated knowledge base of verified findings.

## Important Details
- Knowledge base contains ~200+ ACCEPTED/REJECTED/CHANGED entries accumulated from 2026-08-07 through 2026-08-17
- Rules: passive-only testing (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, secrets committed only as hashes
- 5 models hunt in parallel: Big Pickle, Nemotron 3 Ultra, Longcat, Ling 3.0, Laguna
- Programs: Google VRP (`google.com`, `*.google.com`, `google` GitHub org) and MSRC (`microsoft.com`, `*.microsoft.com`, `*.azure.com`, etc., `microsoft` GitHub org)
- 3 active hypotheses at confidence ≥40 with concrete verify_steps; none on REJECTED list
- 2 drafted reports awaiting human submission: `reports/google-vrp-earthengine-secret.md` and `reports/msrc-two-principal-request.md`

